        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Éluard, Georges Bataille\n- Roles: poet, founder, intellectual, literary figure\n- Organizations: surrealist movement\n- Topics: literature, philosophy, anthropology, economics, sociology, history of art\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Éluard was born as Eugène Émile Paul Grindel on 14 December 1895 and died on 18 November 1952.\n- Georges Bataille was born as Georges Albert Maurice Victor Bataille on 10 September 1897 and died on 9 July 1962.\n- Paul Éluard was a French poet and one of the founders of the surrealist movement.\n- Georges Bataille was a French intellectual and literary figure who worked in literature, philosophy, anthropology, economics, sociology, and history of art.",
